7.2 Live panel: Schottky dark current and internal photoemission
A Schottky diode also responds to photons with \(E_g&gt;h\nu&gt;\Phi_B\): the photon is absorbed by the electrons of the metal, and the hot electrons that cross the barrier are collected (internal photoemission). Fowler’s law gives the yield \(\eta=C_1(h\nu-\Phi_B)^2/h\nu\) with \(C_1\sim0.1\)–\(0.5\) eV⁻¹. It is weak (≈ 1 %), but it lets a silicon chip see the mid-infrared: PtSi/Si (\(\Phi_B\approx0.22\) eV) infrared cameras work in the 3–5 µm window.


